@startuml profiles_and_agents
title paddock: profiles and the agent registry

allowmixing
set separator none
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0

package "profiles.py" {
  class Profile <<dataclass>> {
    name = "custom"
    agent = "claude"
    tools = [git, rg, curl]
    include_system_path = true
    network_presets = [anthropic, github]
    extra_domains = []
    shared_dir = "" (isolated scratch workdir)
    skills = []
    mcp = []
    deny_read = [$HOME/.ssh, $HOME/.aws, $HOME/.gnupg, $HOME/.config/gh]
    extra_allow_write = []
    ..
    allowed_domains() : list[str]
  }
  class "functions" as ProfileFns {
    NETWORK_PRESETS
    TOOL_CANDIDATES
    builtin_profiles()
    load_profiles()
    save_profile(profile)
  }
}

package "agents.py" {
  class AgentSpec <<dataclass>> {
    name
    command
    api_domains
    required_tools (what the command cannot start without)
    auth_read_paths
    config_write_paths
    image (OCI image the msb backend boots; unused by srt)
  }
  class "functions" as AgentFns {
    builtin_agents()
    load_agents()
  }
}

database "$PADDOCK_CONFIG_DIR\n(default $HOME/.config/paddock)" as ConfigDir {
  file "profiles/<name>.json" as ProfileFiles
  file "agents/<key>.json" as AgentFiles
}

ProfileFns --> Profile : builds
AgentFns --> AgentSpec : builds
ProfileFiles --> ProfileFns : load_profiles(): built-ins first,\nthen user files keyed by filename stem\n(a file that will not parse, or holds a\nwrong-typed field, is skipped whole)
ProfileFns --> ProfileFiles : save_profile()
AgentFiles --> AgentFns : load_agents(): a user key replaces\nthe built-in of that key, wholesale\n(no command: skipped)
Profile --> AgentFns : looks up profile.agent

note right of ProfileFns
  NETWORK_PRESETS keys: anthropic, github,
  npm, pypi/uv, go, crates.io, homebrew.
end note

note right of AgentFns
  Built-in keys: claude, codex, opencode,
  aider, gemini, shell.
end note

note bottom of Profile
  allowed_domains() = presets expanded
  + extra_domains + the selected agent's
  api_domains, deduplicated and sorted.
  Nothing else reaches the sandbox allowlist.
end note

note bottom of AgentSpec
  auth_read_paths holds only that agent's own
  credentials. $HOME/.ssh, .aws, .gnupg and
  .config/gh stay in deny_read unless the user
  takes them out (SPEC section 5).

  required_tools go on the srt shim dir with the
  command itself: codex is a script whose shebang
  runs node, and a PATH without node is a pane
  that dies on exit 127. Choosing the agent is
  what puts them there, so the agent list, the
  confirm and --dry-run all name them. An agent
  whose required tool is not on this host reads
  as "(not installed)" and cannot be chosen.
end note

@enduml
